Warning cleanup, Windows code: spelling only, no behaviour change.

The Windows-only counterpart of 0089 and 0091.
- -Wmissing-field-initializers (36 occurrences, d3d12_util.h is included by 12 files): the three
  D3D12_HEAP_PROPERTIES constants spell out the fields they left zero (D3D12_CPU_PAGE_PROPERTY_UNKNOWN and
  D3D12_MEMORY_POOL_UNKNOWN are 0, node masks 0).
- -Wpessimizing-move (d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp): no std::move around a returned temporary.
- -Wsign-compare (d3d12_provider.cpp): d3d12_adapter is compared as uint32_t after the existing >= 0 check.
- -Wunused-lambda-capture (d3d12/command_processor.cpp): kQueryFinished is a constant expression.
- -Winconsistent-missing-override (threading_win.cpp): the GClock SetRepeatingAt overload is marked override like
  its siblings; it already overrode the virtual in rex/thread.h, so the vtable is unchanged.
- -Wmicrosoft-cast (xinput_input_driver.cpp): GetProcAddress results are cast to the void* members explicitly.
- -Wunused-variable: d3d12_immediate_drawer.cpp drops an unused reference to the emplaced upload;
  d3d12_presenter.cpp marks temporal_effect_selected [[maybe_unused]] (only read when FidelityFX is built in).

